          "ruleId": "CWE-674",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "MISSING depth limit on the recursive JSON-writing path. org.eclipse.parsson.JsonGeneratorImpl.write(JsonValue) (line 240) recurses into itself for nested structures -- `write(child)` at line 249 for each JsonArray element and `write(member.getKey(), member.getValue())` at line 257 for each JsonObject member -- with NO recursion-depth guard. The configured depthLimit control is consumed in exactly three places in the whole repository, all of them JsonParserImpl constructors (`new Stack(jsonContext.depthLimit())` at lines 66/72/79, enforced in Stack.push at line 396); JsonGeneratorImpl.java contains ZERO occurrences of 'depth' or 'nested'. Consequently the depth protection covers only text->object parsing, not object->text writing: a deeply nested JsonValue built via JsonObjectBuilderImpl/JsonArrayBuilderImpl (which also never consult depthLimit) and then serialized through JsonWriterImpl/JsonGeneratorImpl.write(JsonValue) produces unbounded recursion and StackOverflowError (CWE-674). write(JsonValue) is attacker-reachable (reachable_from_entry=true, hop_distance=2).\n\nVerifier (CONFIRM): I re-derived the structural claim and it holds exactly. JsonGeneratorImpl.write(JsonValue) (JsonGeneratorImpl.java:240-282) is mutually recursive with write(String, JsonValue) (lines 312-354) over the JsonValue tree -- recursion sites at 249, 257, 323, 331 -- with no recursion-depth counter or limit check in either body. The generator never receives the depth control: its constructors (lines 95-107) take a JsonContext but read only bufferPool(), and a repo-wide grep for depth|depthLimit|MAX_DEPTH over all *.java returns ZERO hits in JsonGeneratorImpl.java/JsonPrettyGeneratorImpl.java. depthLimit() is consumed in exactly three places repo-wide -- the JsonParserImpl constructors at lines 66/72/79 -- and enforced only in JsonParserImpl.Stack.push (lines 394-397). JsonObjectBuilderImpl holds a jsonContext and uses bigIntegerScaleLimit() (lines 89-118) but never depthLimit(). So the nesting control covers text->object parsing only, not object->text writing (CWE-674). Reach is real in source, not just graph-asserted: JsonObjectImpl.toString() (JsonObjectBuilderImpl.java:327-333) -> JsonWriterImpl.write(JsonStructure) -> generator.write(value) (JsonWriterImpl.java:67) -> the recursive method, matching the graph's hop_distance=2 / reachable_from_entry=true. I downgrade severity from the analyst's framing: JsonContext.java:44 sets DEFAULT_MAX_DEPTH=1000 and Stack.push throws at size>=limit, so any PARSED structure is capped under 1000 levels (~1000-2000 frames), which will not normally overflow a default 1MB JVM thread stack; and JsonConfig.java:37-41 documents MAX_DEPTH as applying \"when being parsing JSON string\", so parse-only may be intended scope. Actual StackOverflowError therefore requires a raised org.eclipse.parsson.maxDepth, a structure built via JsonObjectBuilderImpl/JsonArrayBuilderImpl/MapUtil.handle (MapUtil.java:39-69, itself unguarded-recursive) that bypasses the parser entirely, or a small-stack thread. The missing control is genuinely present and reachable, but impact is DoS-only and config/path-conditioned, so LOW. Exploit-reference grounding unavailable: exploit_search returned \"exploit corpus unavailable: not indexed\"."
          },
