          "ruleId": "CWE-344",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Static/constant OAuth 1.0a nonce hardcoded as a literal: `put(\"oauth_nonce\", \"4b25256957d75b6370f33a4501dc5e7e\")` inside the TreeMap initializer in TwitterObjectSearch.getSearchStream, alongside a `// TODO` comment acknowledging it is unfinished. The OAuth 1.0a nonce must be freshly random per request -- its entire purpose is replay protection. Because this value is a compile-time constant, every signed request this code issues reuses the same nonce, so the HMAC-SHA1 signature base string varies only by `oauth_timestamp`, defeating replay detection and making captured requests replayable within the server's timestamp window. The signing key is built at line 117 as `new SecretKeySpec((consumerSecret + \"&\" + accessTokenSecret).getBytes(), \"HmacSHA1\")`.\n\nVerifier (CONFIRM): The construct is genuinely present in the source: TwitterObjectSearch.java:84 contains `put(\"oauth_nonce\", \"4b25256957d75b6370f33a4501dc5e7e\"); // TODO`, a compile-time-constant OAuth 1.0a nonce, and a repo-wide grep for `oauth_nonce` returns only this one site. It does feed the HMAC-SHA1 signature base string (built at lines 93-113 from the same map, signed at 116-119 with the key `new SecretKeySpec((consumerSecret+\"&\"+accessTokenSecret).getBytes(),\"HmacSHA1\")` at line 117), so every request this code signs reuses the same nonce, varying only by `oauth_timestamp` (line 86). That is a real CWE-344 violation of the nonce contract, self-acknowledged by the `// TODO`. TWO CORRECTIONS to the analyst. (1) Location: the `put` is at line 84, not 81 \u2014 line 81 is the start of the anonymous TreeMap initializer, which is merely the line the graph stamps on the synthetic `<init>` node whose `code` property spans the whole block. (2) The impact narrative is inverted and overstated: in OAuth 1.0a the SERVER enforces nonce+timestamp uniqueness, so a client emitting a constant nonce does not defeat the server's replay detection and does not make captured requests replayable \u2014 it causes this client's own requests to be rejected as duplicates within a given timestamp second. No secret leaks and the HMAC key is unaffected. Severity is therefore LOW, not high: the file is a demo CLI whose only EntryPoint is `main(String[])` (graph: kind=handler, method_full_name=org.eclipse.parsson.demos.twitter.TwitterObjectSearch.main), it is excluded from the default Maven build (root pom.xml:438-442 ships only impl/rest/bundles; `demos` appears only in an optional profile's <modules> at pom.xml:466-469), it ships with all four credentials blank in twitterconfig.properties, and it takes zero untrusted input (searchStr is the literal \"#javaone\" at line 68, searchUrl a literal at line 69). Advisory exploit_search was unavailable (\"exploit corpus unavailable: not indexed\"); no versioned third-party component is implicated since the weakness is first-party code."
